Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:27:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] fix(rules): enforce the agreed Hazard rules across
 client, Worker, docs and tests

The agreed gameplay rules for the Hazard (skull) tile are:

- A Hazard always destroys itself.
- Picked with other shapes, it destroys itself and all the other picked
  shapes, including Dummy tiles.
- Picking a Hazard first must not give the same player another chance:
  the Hazard is resolved and the turn ends, switching to the next player
  where applicable.
- Only Play Alone receives the one-point Hazard penalty; the other modes
  never lose points for a Hazard.
- Dummy tiles never incur a score penalty of their own.

The local game already played it this way; the documentation, the pure
rules module, the online Worker and their tests described and enforced
the opposite (harmless first-pick glimpse, versus penalty when real
shapes were picked, free Hazard in Play Alone). Documentation and Worker
behaviour do not override the agreed rules, so they are brought in line
here instead of the game:

- src/rules.js: hazardAction() (first-pick 'hit' routing, never called
  by the scene) is replaced by hazardPenalty(isPlayAlone), which encodes
  that only Play Alone loses a point; GameScene now routes the blast
  penalty through it (versus modes pass 0 and applyPenalty is a no-op).
- worker/src/game-engine.js: a first-pick Hazard now detonates
  immediately (applyHazardBlast) instead of starting the 900 ms
  'hazard-hit' pending glimpse, and applyHazardBlast no longer deducts
  the point when real shapes were picked. Online modes never lose score
  to a Hazard; Dummy + Hazard stays free as before.
- GAMEPLAY.md / README.md / DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md: the Hazard tile section,
  the Play Alone scoring bullet and the developer notes now describe the
  agreed rules (the old text claimed a harmless first-pick glimpse, a
  1-point versus blast and a free Play Alone Hazard - all removed).
- tests: rules.test.js pins hazardPenalty; the Worker tests now pin
  "first pick destroys itself and ends the turn", "blast after shapes
  destroys them without a penalty" and the new "Dummy tiles are
  destroyed but never cost points of their own".
